{
 "id": "SHW-15",
 "name": "headphone-configurator",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "A 3D product configurator: headphones to turn, recolour and explode",
 "summary": "Wireless headphones built from 21 lit 3D draws of nine primitives (extruded arcs for the band, pad and yokes, a capped lathe for each cup, tori, cones, cylinders) turn slowly on a turntable; a drag orbits the camera, four swatches cross-fade the shell and cushion colours, and Explode eases the parts apart while five labels, projected from 3D in the same canvas, follow their parts on the nearer cup. A fitBox swaps a phone layout (title above, swatch card below) for a tablet one (a side panel with specs), and the 3D framing follows.",
 "prompt": "Make a product configurator for our Aura One headphones: a 3D model on a turntable people can drag round, colour swatches that repaint it, and an explode button that pulls the parts apart with labels. It should work on a phone (swatches under the model) and a tablet (a side panel).",
 "level": 5,
 "family": "SHW",
 "hand_built": "Scene3D has no runtime colour or explode toggle and no projected labels: the camera orbit, the colour cross-fade (computed argb colours from float arrays) and the label projection are written by hand.",
 "capabilities": {
  "primary": [
